<title>UK: Parkwood Holdings shares set debut premium.</title>
<headline>Parkwood Holdings shares set debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Britain's Parkwood Holdings Plc rose to a premium in active trading as they made their debut on the London Stock Exchange on Tuesday.</p>
<p>By 1030 GMT shares in the facilities management company were quoted at 75p with 1.7 million shares traded, after being placed with institutional investors at 65p by broker Wise Speke.</p>
<p>At the issue price Parkwood was valued at 14.0 million stg. The float raised 5.5 million stg for the company.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
